// C-interop (D-012, Y8b4b): this program calls functions implemented in C (gcc).
// The Cyan definitions of the c_* functions are deliberately wrong stubs that give the
// compiler their signatures; scripts/test_abi_interop.sh weakens them so the C
// definitions win at link time. Exit code N means check N failed.
// SKIP-TEST: part of scripts/test_abi_interop.sh (needs the C object)

